# personal

There are some faces that are impossible to forget.

Geto's is one of them.

That is why this is so difficult to look at.

I knew him.

I knew the way he spoke.

I knew the way he smiled.

I knew what he believed in.

I knew the person behind the face.

The thing standing in Shibuya had his face.

That should have been enough.

It wasn't.

There was something wrong in the eyes.

Not physically.

Something harder to describe.

Recognition works both ways.

I recognized him.

He recognized that I recognized him.

But whatever was looking back at me was not Suguru Geto.

I don't think it ever was.
